
Create a Custom Color Profile (Built-in Method) (For MacOS)

You can manually lower your screen's white point using the hidden Display Calibrator Assistant:
1. Open System Settings > Displays.
2. Click the Color profile dropdown menu and select Customize...
3. Hold down the Option key on your keyboard and click the + button.
4. Click Continue through the intro screens until you reach Target White Point.
5. Uncheck Use native white point and drag the slider to the left (around D50 gives a much softer, paper-like white instead of harsh daylight).
6. Name and save your profile—you can switch back to the default profile anytime from the Displays menu.


